==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|nl|kooi}} or {{bor|ru|gml|kōje}}, ultimately from {{der|ru|la|cavea}}. In sense of a normal bed when used in informal speech compare {{cog|sv|krypa till kojs}} and {{cog|nn|krypa til køys}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ко́йка}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-койка.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|ко́йка|*}}

# {{lb|ru|nautical}} [[bunk]], [[hammock]]
## {{lb|ru|by extension}} [[berth]] in a passenger train
##: {{ux|ru|многие пассажиры уже послезали со своих коек|many passengers have already come down from their berths}}
##: {{syn|ru|полка}}
# {{lb|ru|healthcare}} [[hospital]] [[bed]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[реанемационный|реанимацио́нная]] [[пала́та]] [[на]] 12 '''ко́ек'''|subst=12//двена́дцать|a 12-'''bed''' resuscitation room}}
# {{lb|ru|informal}} [[cot]], [[bed]]; any [[sleeping]] [[furniture]] for use by one person
#: {{ux|ru|мне пора в койку|it's time for me to hit the hay}}
#: {{ux|ru|запрыгнуть кому-то в койку|to have sex with somebody [usually a man]}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|ко́йка|*}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ru|гама́к}}
* {{l|ru|койко-ме́сто}}

